<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kakegawa Castle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kakegawa Castle is a Japanese castle in Kakegawa, Shizuoka Prefecture, in the former province of Tōtōmi. Built in the early 16th century by a retainer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-clan">Imagawa clan</a>, it was where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imagawa-ujizane">Imagawa Ujizane</a> held out against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> before surrendering in 1569. Its keep, wrecked by an earthquake in 1854, was rebuilt in wood in 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kakegawa-castle.jpg" alt="Kakegawa Castle" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ShizuokaSensei at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kakegawacastleapril2006.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
